2. **Error hunt:** A fictional student forgot a label and wrote only “44.” What question should you ask them before accepting the number?

## Independent practice

Complete each item with visible work. Aim for clear diagrams + checked answers.

1. At an East Texas trail hike, Maya walks 1/3 mile then 1/5 mile. How far did she walk in all? Estimate first, then compute with a common denominator.
2. At Prosper Prep basketball practice, Maya walks 2/4 mile then 3/7 mile. How far did she walk in all? Estimate first, then compute with a common denominator.
3. At a library reading challenge, Maya walks 3/5 mile then 1/6 mile. How far did she walk in all? Estimate first, then compute with a common denominator.
4. At a youth-group picnic, Maya walks 5/6 mile then 1/8 mile. How far did she walk in all? Estimate first, then compute with a common denominator.
5. At a science-fair supply run, Maya walks 1/2 mile then 4/5 mile. How far did she walk in all? Estimate first, then compute with a common denominator.
