## Independent practice

Complete each item with visible work. Aim for clear diagrams + checked answers.

1. 45 students are 25% of those who signed up for Prosper Prep basketball practice. How many signed up in all? (Solve part = pct% × whole.)
2. 132 students are 30% of those who signed up for an East Texas trail hike. How many signed up in all? (Solve part = pct% × whole.)
3. 143 students are 35% of those who signed up for a scholarship bake sale. How many signed up in all? (Solve part = pct% × whole.)
4. 84 students are 40% of those who signed up for a band concert ticket table. How many signed up in all? (Solve part = pct% × whole.)
5. 99 students are 45% of those who signed up for a Saturday soccer tournament. How many signed up in all? (Solve part = pct% × whole.)
6. 187 students are 20% of those who signed up for a science-fair supply run. How many signed up in all? (Solve part = pct% × whole.)

### Answer key (try first)

*Check your work only after you attempt each item. Show your representation, not only the final number.*

1. whole = 45 ÷ (25/100) = 180.00.
2. whole = 132 ÷ (30/100) = 440.00.
3. whole = 143 ÷ (35/100) = 408.57.
4. whole = 84 ÷ (40/100) = 210.00.
5. whole = 99 ÷ (45/100) = 220.00.
6. whole = 187 ÷ (20/100) = 935.00.

